# Better Solution (Your Solution)

```python
class Solution:
    def smallestPalindrome(self, s: str) -> str:
        s = list(s)

        n = len(s)
        mid = n // 2

        s[:mid] = sorted(s[:mid])

        for i in range(mid):
            s[n - 1 - i] = s[i]

        return "".join(s)
```

---

# Why does this work?

This solution uses one very important property.

## Property

The input string is **already a palindrome**.

Example

```
daccad
```

Left half

```
dac
```

Right half

```
cad
```

Notice

```
Right half = reverse(left half)
```

If we rearrange only the **left half**, then simply mirror it to the right side.

The palindrome property is automatically preserved.

So we only need to make the **left half as small as possible**.

The smallest arrangement is simply

```
sort(left half)
```

Then mirror it.

